  "body": "Found while fixing #89. The lathe Facing kind faces the part model, not the stock above it: with the part at its finished length it reports \"nothing to face\", so a bar's facing allowance declared in the setup stock cannot be faced off. Turning a bar to length - the first op on most lathe jobs - is therefore not expressible from stock, and drilling after facing (#89) can only be tested by modelling the allowance on the part.\n\nDone means: Lathe Facing removes the stock above the part's end face (from the setup stock to the part's end), refusing by name when there is neither stock allowance nor part material to face; pinned by a bar with a 2 mm facing allowance in the stock that faces to the part end and lets a following axial drill post.",
